WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:18.873
When Olivia arrived on Saturday, Katie was sitting on the front porch.

2
00:00:18.874 --> 00:00:21.809
She was moving her foot in the air.

3
00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:25.384
"What are you doing?" asked Olivia.

4
00:00:25.385 --> 00:00:26.674
"Check this out.

5
00:00:26.675 --> 00:00:30.077
What does this spell?" said Katie.

6
00:00:30.078 --> 00:00:35.487
Olivia's eyes followed Katie's toes as they moved through the air.

7
00:00:35.488 --> 00:00:38.737
"That was an A," explained Katie.

8
00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:42.457
"This is a B. Watch carefully."

9
00:00:42.458 --> 00:00:45.546
She moved her foot around some more.

10
00:00:45.547 --> 00:00:50.996
"Dr. Howarth says I have to write the alphabet several times each day.

11
00:00:50.997 --> 00:00:54.085
If I do, my ankle will get strong.

12
00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:57.798
Then I can go to the hayride on Friday."

13
00:00:57.799 --> 00:01:01.536
"Great!" said Olivia. "You keep writing.

14
00:01:01.537 --> 00:01:03.989
I'll go pick up walnuts."

15
00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:09.554
"Don't let the ticks bite you!" said Katie. Olivia laughed.

16
00:01:09.555 --> 00:01:13.702
Joy had been collecting walnuts since after breakfast.

17
00:01:13.703 --> 00:01:18.560
When she saw Olivia jogging up the hill, she ran to meet her.

18
00:01:18.561 --> 00:01:23.190
"Here I am! Ready to help!" said Olivia.

19
00:01:23.191 --> 00:01:27.119
"Thank you!" Joy pulled her over to the cart.

20
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:32.073
"There are a million walnuts under these trees," she said.

21
00:01:32.074 --> 00:01:33.772
"See how many I've picked up?

22
00:01:33.773 --> 00:01:38.240
Dad says when the cart's full, we can go to the nut-buying station.

23
00:01:38.241 --> 00:01:41.217
Then we can fill it up again!"

24
00:01:41.218 --> 00:01:45.623
"Let's see who can fill her bucket first!" said Olivia.

25
00:01:45.624 --> 00:01:48.863
She picked up two walnuts at once.

26
00:01:48.864 --> 00:01:56.538
For several minutes, the only sound was the thud, thud, thud of walnuts dropping into buckets.

27
00:01:56.539 --> 00:02:00.395
"Done!" said Joy. "I win!"

28
00:02:00.396 --> 00:02:03.352
"Let's do it again!" said Olivia.

29
00:02:03.353 --> 00:02:10.870
They emptied their buckets into the cart and started grabbing more walnuts. Thud, thud, thud.

30
00:02:10.871 --> 00:02:14.390
"Done!" cried Olivia. "It's a tie!"

31
00:02:14.391 --> 00:02:17.273
The girls laughed.

32
00:02:17.274 --> 00:02:20.942
They were working, but it was fun!

33
00:02:20.943 --> 00:02:26.195
As the morning sun rose higher, Joy moved closer to the woods.

34
00:02:26.196 --> 00:02:31.760
Olivia worked her way toward the pond, filling bucket after bucket.

35
00:02:31.761 --> 00:02:35.901
"The grass is kind of tall there," Joy called.

36
00:02:35.902 --> 00:02:38.485
"It's a good spot," said Olivia.

37
00:02:38.486 --> 00:02:42.069
"Lots of walnuts have rolled down here."

38
00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:45.308
"Just watch out," said Joy.

39
00:02:45.309 --> 00:02:48.667
"Watch out for what?" said Olivia.

40
00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:51.517
"Oh, poison ivy and stuff.

41
00:02:51.518 --> 00:02:54.561
Ticks. You know. Whatever."

42
00:02:54.562 --> 00:02:59.203
Olivia was picking up walnuts as fast as she could.

43
00:02:59.204 --> 00:03:01.292
She filled her bucket quickly.

44
00:03:01.293 --> 00:03:06.752
"I'm going to set a new world record!" she said with a laugh.

45
00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:10.102
Then she screamed.

46
00:03:10.103 --> 00:03:12.379
"A snake!" she yelled.

47
00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:16.560
She tried to stand up, but she slipped back down into the grass.

48
00:03:16.561 --> 00:03:21.906
She screamed again.

49
00:03:21.907 --> 00:03:25.707
"It's just a black snake," called Joy.

50
00:03:25.708 --> 00:03:26.876
"There it goes.

51
00:03:26.877 --> 00:03:29.186
See? You scared it."

52
00:03:29.187 --> 00:03:32.709
"I scared the snake?" cried Olivia.

53
00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:35.223
She ran toward Joy.

54
00:03:35.224 --> 00:03:39.552
Just then a strong breeze blew through the trees.

55
00:03:39.553 --> 00:03:43.194
A walnut fell on Olivia's toe.

56
00:03:43.195 --> 00:03:47.273
"Ouch!" she cried and looked up into the tree.

57
00:03:47.274 --> 00:03:50.668
A walnut fell right on her nose!

58
00:03:50.669 --> 00:03:53.379
"Oh! That really hurt!"

59
00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:58.335
She rubbed her nose and screamed again.

60
00:03:58.336 --> 00:04:01.316
"My nose is bleeding!"

61
00:04:01.317 --> 00:04:06.005
Soon Olivia was sitting beside Katie on the front porch.

62
00:04:06.006 --> 00:04:10.285
"Keep holding your nose for ten minutes," said Grandpa.

63
00:04:10.286 --> 00:04:14.678
"And no more walnut collecting today," Mom said.

64
00:04:14.679 --> 00:04:18.063
"You shouldn't bend over for several hours."

65
00:04:18.064 --> 00:04:22.996
"Another damaged walnut picker," said Katie.

66
00:04:22.997 --> 00:04:29.139
Joy was heading back out for more walnuts when Dad's truck drove up the driveway.

67
00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:34.679
Joy stopped and talked with him for a moment, and then continued toward the pond.

68
00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:38.815
Dad joined the rest of the family on the porch.

69
00:04:38.816 --> 00:04:41.322
"Bad news for Joy," he said.

70
00:04:41.323 --> 00:04:46.328
"This morning the nut company lowered the price again—to ten cents."

71
00:04:46.329 --> 00:04:50.073
"Oh, poor Joy!" said Mom.

72
00:04:50.074 --> 00:04:51.917
Grandpa shook his head.

73
00:04:51.918 --> 00:04:54.641
"She's running out of time," he said.

74
00:04:54.642 --> 00:04:57.812
"Do you think she can still reach her goal?"

75
00:04:57.813 --> 00:05:00.301
"I don't know," said Dad.

76
00:05:00.302 --> 00:05:03.490
"Now she needs more than five hundred pounds."

77
00:05:03.491 --> 00:05:07.966
"Now she needs a lot more helpers," said Katie.

78
00:05:07.967 --> 00:05:11.237
Olivia pulled her cell phone out of her pocket.

79
00:05:11.238 --> 00:05:17.123
"Now we need to make some phone calls!"
